    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 48,
        "text": "Hi, Ben. You look busy. What are you doing?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "8da372a21cfdfbe259129a36698c1aad2f5f1c42061cc6bf75080b2ac931ead4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 54,
        "sourceEnd": 141,
        "text": "I’m looking at the library’s new plan. They want to change how people find information.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "2ab2d4abe1ace18a83d8fa840fe0b1c267cc09d718d479067cacf18a272eed77",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 147,
        "sourceEnd": 172,
        "text": "Really? What’s different?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "8b63930995f30eb229f29d7aa5b25ee7e760bc9bd59dddf5556240e3149795e9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 178,
        "sourceEnd": 331,
        "text": "Last year, there were only two computers near the entrance. Now there are eight. That means more people can use the internet and search for books online.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "be6f8935ea224451f7c4e0dca201c5208d946e3988c51d604a40fbf90006c501",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 337,
        "sourceEnd": 375,
        "text": "That’s a big change. What about books?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "8e8ba1e3bb1460b59f0ef7d5ed16934808abf883306b7d9e8b10b5ebcd26e5b2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 381,
        "sourceEnd": 542,
        "text": "The number of printed books fell by 15 percent. But the number of e-books rose by 40 percent. So the library has fewer physical books but many more digital ones.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "f811cfcdb5ffd8ac26617263919beda8bf770b23d5d2d666b6bea170a26aa63c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 548,
        "sourceEnd": 575,
        "text": "So more people read online?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "0d57e9a810305b3432f75b01294ba12ef8080ec4c80ab3fe915f58a714895590",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 581,
        "sourceEnd": 701,
        "text": "Yes. In 2022, 30 percent of visitors used e-books. Last month, 55 percent did. That’s a big increase in digital reading.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "e4758a66e4fb97a5018f4803fbd02e7a50ff07feb652fcb1ad6faa0b0066d5d7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 707,
        "sourceEnd": 732,
        "text": "And the quiet study area?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "f0b986abd0c68caafa17f890dcbc36e3b19fd9583813ecd8baf62c24ddbdfba4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 738,
        "sourceEnd": 832,
        "text": "It’s smaller now. There were 40 desks before. Now there are 25. That’s a decrease of 15 desks.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "cccc7be3464bc8215cd064de2417282ee526894b97687246f21e961d3a0a6b36",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 838,
        "sourceEnd": 842,
        "text": "Why?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "5d8a995a6fa7cf7c577cc9d49ca9e00d4aee4d0bcd5e2ad5caff27e2a8097276",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 848,
        "sourceEnd": 985,
        "text": "Because more students study in groups. The group room is bigger. It went from 10 seats to 18 seats. So there’s more space for group work.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "400de2c3813a59a03765d7f0020fdf1cc727e9335c7dd82319c1902bedbd4955",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 991,
        "sourceEnd": 1030,
        "text": "I see. Did the library buy more chairs?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "62d84ee531a79ceaa0a28e75a55c2912e002f1cf775e805c1c79cf5f9d2c8d9b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1036,
        "sourceEnd": 1113,
        "text": "Yes, but fewer than before. They bought 20 chairs last year and 12 this year.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "559b9a166232745e1b6efb752a3922ed19a218b633391aabb5f8cbfee1bd40f7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1119,
        "sourceEnd": 1166,
        "text": "Wait, that’s fewer? I thought they bought more.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "153bb8d0a3fd2bbf377caeaea3ca00baebb14c9a366f92f32def53bb67ad4676",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1172,
        "sourceEnd": 1249,
        "text": "No, fewer. Sorry, I said that wrong. They bought 12 chairs this year, not 20.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "2d5d2bf2bf09c2fd4b78c5c739f46c5c318366b8ad291820c3e35a250072d34f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1255,
        "sourceEnd": 1300,
        "text": "OK. So the library is changing. Is it better?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "c620af07da670ed1b5cd1d27b0dffaf0541f91eee46c48931d9bbeb614f1f18b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1306,
        "sourceEnd": 1410,
        "text": "Maybe. The number of visitors increased by 8 percent. But some older people miss the printed newspapers.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "43cad23de695bc49c45f732e12f21bab79819ae6d6eabec40fe4a2189fc0426d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1416,
        "sourceEnd": 1447,
        "text": "Did they remove the newspapers?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "9f1d3e6bb2050d28e02be77f6a05f1fbded0adb79457e8bd05a8a23715a1b700",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1453,
        "sourceEnd": 1530,
        "text": "Not all. There were 12 newspapers before. Now there are 5. That’s a big drop.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "ebdfadbc35d5b662bd2ee5bc9c6207e0b6f49671f6a09d2a3311823c4125108f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1536,
        "sourceEnd": 1561,
        "text": "What about the help desk?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "a76ec2c4e4eb791c39eeac651cdc84353f9de0dd4b7169d6b53f8c324720d74d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1567,
        "sourceEnd": 1659,
        "text": "It’s still there, but it’s smaller. There was one large desk. Now there are two small desks.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "9be9d9883e8f175882b8ccddf0f8a701e133edde06031ad8ad4f4c26330995ab",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1665,
        "sourceEnd": 1701,
        "text": "Two small desks? That’s interesting.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "0ea0112212a12e1a349c542841c3c20d392bfb1f7c2163acf78abf1b1cac6895",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1707,
        "sourceEnd": 1817,
        "text": "Yes. And the library now has a map near the door. It shows where everything is. So it’s easier to find things.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "1f8acb334f429a8528e3d20748a5fa27f757802b35c8a0dd97395b2293a85b88",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1823,
        "sourceEnd": 1861,
        "text": "Good. I think I’ll visit this weekend.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "74d1500ad1919f704875633cfa6cb3e68d63265c3f8b59f4e6c3ca222b3a9ea0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1867,
        "sourceEnd": 1893,
        "text": "Me too. Let’s go together.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "f43a6ef111efa53305e2387963f53736f536f11ce35c4dd03243df1596a73bb5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
